{{also|Gherkin}}
==English==
[[File:PicklingCucumbers.jpg|thumb]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{l|en|gerkin}} {{qualifier|chiefly archaic}}

===Etymology===
From earlier Dutch plural of ''gurk'' (="cucumber"), shortened form of East Frisian{{attention|stq}} ''augurk''<sup>[http://www.etymonline.com/index.php?term=gherkin]</sup>

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|GenAm}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɝkɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{a|RP}} {{IPA|/ˈɡɜːkɪn/|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɜː(ɹ)kɪn|lang=en}}
* {{hyphenation|gher|kin|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A small [[cucumber]], often [[pickle]]d whole.

